        <Comment>
            <Line>Switching losses (Eon and Eoff) are given in Figures 21 and 22 in the datasheet for Vdd = 1000V and 1200V, respectively, and for Tj = 25C, and Rg = 0.5Ω. The data is then scaled based on the user-specified value of Rg using the data in Figure 23, as well as the measured junction temperature during the simulation, using the data in Figure 25 (note that Eoff is not affected by temperature).</Line>
            <Line></Line>
            <Line>* The user should choose a Rg value between 0.5Ω and 6Ω, with a default value of 0.5Ω.</Line>
            <Line></Line>
            <Line>MOSFET conduction losses are given for Vgson = 15V in Figure 1 in the datasheet for Tj = 25C, with data at Vgson = 18V additionally provided by GeneSiC. The data in Figure 5 for Rdson vs. T is then used to calculate a more accurate temperature dependence on these specific losses.</Line>
            <Line></Line>
            <Line>* The user should choose a Vgson value of 15V or 18V.</Line>
            <Line></Line>
            <Line>Body diode conduction losses are given for Vgsoff = 0V, -3V and -5V using data in Figures 17 and 18 in the datasheet at 25C and 175C, respectively.</Line>
            <Line></Line>
            <Line>* The user should choose a Vgsoff value of 0V, -3V or -5V.</Line>
            <Line></Line>
            <Line>The information above is based on datasheet Rev 21/May.</Line>
